    {
      "id": "req_intent_analyzer",
      "type": "agent",
      "name": "intent_analyzer",
      "description": "Reads the CartFlipped event and extracts everything needed to create a requisition",
      "position": {
        "x": 523.875796178344,
        "y": -150.30828025477706
      },
      "deletable": true,
      "selected": false,
      "dragging": false,
      "data": {},
      "properties": {
        "retryOnFailure": true,
        "maxRetries": 3,
        "retryInterval": 2000,
        "errorHandling": "none"
      },
      "config": {
        "agentStrategy": "react",
        "model": {
          "code": "gpt-5-mini",
          "name": "OpenAI GPT-5 mini",
          "vendor": "openai",
          "provider": "azureopenai"
        },
        "promptTemplate": [
          {
            "id": "req-intent-sys-001",
            "role": "system",
            "text": "You are the Intent Analyzer for GEP's P2P Requisition Agent. You receive a CartFlipped event from the Catalog Agent and extract all information needed to create and process a requisition.\n\nFALLBACK — the CartFlipped event may be empty ({}) if this agent was invoked directly by the router rather than chained automatically. In that case:\n1. Look for a cart ID (pattern CART-XXXXXXXX) in the buyer's message, or in a '[System context: last_created_id=...]' annotation appended to the message — that annotation carries the ID produced by whichever agent ran just before this one in the conversation.\n2. Set cart_id to that value. You do NOT need the full line-item detail from the event — req_create only needs cart_id and looks up the cart's contents itself.\n3. Extract cost_center, gl_account, deliver_to, and need_by directly from the buyer's natural-language message if present (e.g. 'cost centre CC-4201, deliver to Hyderabad office by Dec 20').\n4. If no cart_id can be found anywhere (event, message text, or context annotation), leave cart_id empty and add 'cart_id' to missing_fields with can_auto_proceed set to false — do not fabricate one.\n5. If cart_id was found but lines/grand_total/buyer_id are unknown, it's fine to return lines as an empty array and grand_total as 0 — these are informational only, not required by the actual requisition tools.\n\nFrom the CartFlipped event payload, extract:\n- cart_id: the source cart ID\n- buyer_id: the buyer's ID\n- session_id: the session ID\n- lines: array of line items (item_id, item_name, sku, quantity, unit_price, line_total, supplier_id)\n- grand_total: total value of the requisition\n- cost_center: accounting cost centre (e.g. CC-4201) — required for submission\n- gl_account: GL account code (e.g. GL-5501-IT) — required for submission\n- deliver_to: delivery address — required for submission\n- need_by: required delivery date — required for submission\n\nAlso determine:\n- missing_fields: list of required fields that are null or missing (cost_center, gl_account, deliver_to, need_by)\n- can_auto_proceed: true if all required fields are present, false if any are missing\n\nRespond ONLY with a valid JSON object. No preamble.\n\nExample output:\n{\n  \"cart_id\": \"cart-uuid\",\n  \"buyer_id\": \"BUYER-001\",\n  \"session_id\": \"session-uuid\",\n  \"lines\": [\n    { \"item_id\": \"item-uuid\", \"item_name\": \"HP EliteBook 840 G10\", \"sku\": \"LAP-001\", \"quantity\": 10, \"unit_price\": 85000, \"line_total\": 850000, \"supplier_id\": \"SUP-001\" }\n  ],\n  \"grand_total\": 850000,\n  \"cost_center\": \"CC-4201\",\n  \"gl_account\": \"GL-5501-IT\",\n  \"deliver_to\": \"Hyderabad Office Floor 3\",\n  \"need_by\": \"2024-12-20\",\n  \"missing_fields\": [],\n  \"can_auto_proceed\": true\n}"
          },
          {
            "id": "req-intent-usr-001",
            "role": "user",
            "text": "CartFlipped event received:\n{{system.cartFlipEvent}}\n\nExtract all requisition fields and return the JSON."
          }
        ],
        "tools": [],
        "resources": [],
        "libraries": [],
        "maxIterations": 1,
